WEBVTT

01:02.560 --> 01:09.560
<b><i>Betrayal - Shock</i></b>

01:06.270 --> 01:08.900
Strange mutant phenomenon
in the Tohoku region?

01:10.110 --> 01:11.860
Have you noticed anything?

01:12.190 --> 01:13.990
Nothing in particular.

01:14.530 --> 01:20.410
And it's silly to assume that a mutant did what
you described to that bridge and river.

01:21.120 --> 01:25.290
Still, the mutant tracking system
that the U-Men were using

01:25.290 --> 01:27.290
was giving off significant readings.

01:28.290 --> 01:30.040
I can't understand that.

01:32.840 --> 01:34.300
But I'm surprised.

01:34.720 --> 01:37.680
Little Hisako is a member
of the X-Men now.

01:38.050 --> 01:43.180
When I remembered the Sasaki Institute,
Professor X was happy, too.

01:43.980 --> 01:45.020
Charles was...

01:48.150 --> 01:50.940
ls Professor X coming
to Japan as well?

01:51.440 --> 01:51.940
No.

01:52.400 --> 01:54.400
He left the investigation to us.

01:55.030 --> 01:55.700
I see.

01:56.400 --> 01:58.110
What is the Sasaki Academy?

01:59.280 --> 02:02.450
It was never as big
as the Xavier Institute.

02:02.450 --> 02:07.250
I was simply looking after
local mutant children.

02:08.170 --> 02:10.380
Does that mean
you're a mutant, too?

02:11.590 --> 02:12.250
No.

02:12.710 --> 02:14.300
Then why?

02:15.010 --> 02:18.260
I wanted to do something for
the children who were treated coldly

02:18.260 --> 02:22.430
just because they were mutants,
and couldn't attend ordinary school.

02:23.560 --> 02:24.220
But...

02:25.560 --> 02:28.270
There was a limit to
what I could do by myself.

02:28.850 --> 02:30.270
Which is why you closed it?

02:30.900 --> 02:31.650
Yes.

02:32.400 --> 02:35.940
Now I do medical research
pertaining to mutants.

02:37.360 --> 02:39.280
Say, Dr. Sasaki...

02:39.280 --> 02:43.240
I was really good friends with
a kid in school.

02:43.240 --> 02:44.740
A good friend?

02:45.040 --> 02:45.790
Yeah.

02:45.790 --> 02:50.830
I think a little younger, a boy...

02:51.460 --> 02:54.000
But I'm having
trouble remembering.

02:55.090 --> 02:56.760
Do you remember him?

02:58.010 --> 03:02.010
Back then I had
so many children here.

03:02.010 --> 03:03.470
I'm afraid I don't.

03:06.720 --> 03:07.390
Doctor!

03:08.140 --> 03:09.980
It's time for the meeting.

03:10.850 --> 03:14.070
These are the members
of my research team.

03:14.070 --> 03:15.110
From the left there's,

03:15.110 --> 03:16.480
Koichi Kaga,

03:17.320 --> 03:18.570
Jun Sanada,

03:19.360 --> 03:20.700
and Riko Nirasaki.

03:21.820 --> 03:23.320
These are the X-Men.

03:23.910 --> 03:25.660
I've heard all about you.

03:26.120 --> 03:27.500
It's an honor to meet you all!

03:28.370 --> 03:30.000
Is that everybody?

03:30.000 --> 03:30.670
Yes.

03:31.500 --> 03:32.580
Go ahead.

03:33.290 --> 03:34.250
Excuse us.

03:35.500 --> 03:37.510
The storm's died down...

03:38.170 --> 03:40.300
It might be a good time to
go check on the Blackbird.

03:40.970 --> 03:44.100
Do you have anything for getting rid
of ice we could borrow?

03:44.680 --> 03:45.430
Certainly.

03:45.430 --> 03:46.760
I'm going too.

03:47.310 --> 03:48.520
I will, too.

03:49.020 --> 03:49.810
Scott.

03:50.480 --> 03:53.810
You should stay here with
Emma and Hisako.

03:55.440 --> 03:56.440
However...

04:00.740 --> 04:01.700
Understood.

04:10.330 --> 04:13.750
The research facility is in
the back of this house.

04:14.460 --> 04:16.540
The main equipment
is underground.

04:17.840 --> 04:19.090
A boy...

04:19.880 --> 04:22.010
Younger than me...

04:22.380 --> 04:23.180
Hisako.

04:24.010 --> 04:27.470
You used to go to
an ordinary school, right?

04:27.930 --> 04:28.470
Yeah.

04:29.020 --> 04:32.020
I used to come to the Academy
after my regular school let out.

04:33.270 --> 04:36.610
Maybe that boy was
a friend of yours at school?

04:37.570 --> 04:38.730
Maybe...

04:39.780 --> 04:40.780
By the way, Yui.

04:41.940 --> 04:44.570
Aren't you an acquaintance
of Professor X?

04:45.360 --> 04:45.990
Yes.

04:46.490 --> 04:50.500
It was more than 15 years ago,
but I did meet him once.

04:51.040 --> 04:52.710
More than 15 years ago?

04:53.250 --> 04:56.250
But we were never close.

04:57.170 --> 05:00.710
It was such a long time ago,
I don't really remember.

05:01.460 --> 05:05.380
I have to go to a meeting,
so please make yourselves at home.

05:10.060 --> 05:12.600
If you need anything,
you can reach me on this intercom.

05:22.110 --> 05:25.570
I feel like Dr. Sasaki's changed.

05:25.950 --> 05:26.740
Changed?

05:27.160 --> 05:27.950
Yeah.

05:28.370 --> 05:32.870
She used to be kinder
and warmer, I think.

05:33.500 --> 05:35.870
She still seems kind,

05:35.870 --> 05:37.250
at least to me.

05:38.000 --> 05:40.590
That's true, but...

05:42.090 --> 05:44.340
Yui Sasaki is lying.

05:45.260 --> 05:50.470
She said she hasn't seen
Professor X in 15 years.

05:50.970 --> 05:53.930
But she has seen
him since then.

05:54.890 --> 05:56.730
Did you read her mind?

05:59.860 --> 06:01.770
It's because of things like that

06:01.770 --> 06:03.650
that people hate mutants.

06:04.150 --> 06:04.820
No.

06:05.240 --> 06:06.820
I didn't use telepathy.

06:08.110 --> 06:11.700
This is a woman's intuition, right?

06:12.200 --> 06:13.370
A woman's intuition?

06:14.330 --> 06:17.830
When we mentioned
the Professor,

06:18.330 --> 06:19.750
she called him "Charles."

06:20.330 --> 06:23.300
Even though they
weren't that close.

06:23.630 --> 06:27.170
Some people use first names
even with people they're not friendly with.

06:27.680 --> 06:32.890
But she had asked you
if Professor X was planning on coming.

06:33.510 --> 06:38.100
Yui Sasaki is involved with Professor X
on a much deeper level.

06:40.150 --> 06:41.610
A deeper level...

06:49.610 --> 06:51.410
All right, let's pull it out!

06:51.910 --> 06:53.160
That's impossible.

06:53.580 --> 06:54.740
I'm joking.

06:55.330 --> 06:55.950
Storm!

06:56.540 --> 06:58.330
Could you melt all this ice?

06:58.920 --> 07:00.080
That's also impossible.

07:00.420 --> 07:02.170
Look at this snow.

07:02.750 --> 07:04.710
I wonder if you could
even call it snow.

07:07.300 --> 07:09.720
At first glance,
it seems like snow, but...

07:09.720 --> 07:10.590
It doesn't melt.

07:10.590 --> 07:11.680
It's not even cold.

07:12.260 --> 07:14.930
It seems more like a mineral.

07:16.520 --> 07:20.230
So in Japan they have
diamond or ruby snow?

07:20.230 --> 07:21.980
Of course not.

07:23.480 --> 07:26.280
It's as if just this place was
suddenly changed.

07:26.900 --> 07:29.280
At any rate, there's nothing
we can do like this.

07:29.900 --> 07:33.450
I'll contact Charles and have him
send a spare Blackbird.

07:37.080 --> 07:38.410
Yui Sasaki?

07:39.000 --> 07:39.500
<i>Yes.</i>

07:40.160 --> 07:42.830
<i>I thought you should know.</i>

07:43.500 --> 07:44.210
Understood.

07:44.670 --> 07:48.300
In any event, I'll send you
the backup jet at once.

07:48.800 --> 07:49.550
<i>I appreciate it.</i>

07:58.520 --> 07:59.600
<i>It's been a while.</i>

08:00.480 --> 08:01.190
Yui.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.610
I wasn't expecting you
to contact me.

08:05.190 --> 08:06.570
<i>From the sound of it,</i>

08:07.150 --> 08:09.820
you've already <i>heard</i>
a report about me.

08:11.150 --> 08:13.450
<i>I hear you closed the Academy.</i>

08:13.820 --> 08:15.200
I'll get to the point.

08:16.160 --> 08:19.160
I want to continue
my research here in peace.

08:19.870 --> 08:21.330
<i>Are you saying the X-Men
are in the way?</i>

08:22.420 --> 08:24.080
I'll help if needed.

08:24.790 --> 08:28.050
But I want them out of here as soon as
the investigation is over.

08:28.630 --> 08:31.220
<i>Would something be disturbed
if they stay too long?</i>

08:33.130 --> 08:37.810
<i>It may be the key
to solving the string</i>

08:37.810 --> 08:40.020
<i>of mutant occurrences
around your lab</i>

08:40.020 --> 08:41.560
I have nothing to do with it.

08:42.310 --> 08:43.940
I'm not so sure about that.

08:43.940 --> 08:46.020
When I sent
my mind to Tohoku,

08:46.020 --> 08:48.020
I caught a glimpse of
your consciousness,

08:48.020 --> 08:49.030
<i>and a young boy.</i>

08:50.150 --> 08:51.690
<i>I couldn't see his face,</i>

08:52.190 --> 08:54.740
<i>but you overlapped with him.</i>

08:55.450 --> 08:58.120
<i>Does that boy have
anything to do with you?</i>

08:58.740 --> 09:01.040
<i>Why did he enter my mind?</i>

09:03.460 --> 09:04.580
<i>Answer me, Yui.</i>

09:06.580 --> 09:09.300
<i>That boy is probably Takeo.</i>

09:09.710 --> 09:10.500
Takeo?

09:12.970 --> 09:13.720
<i>He's my son.</i>

09:14.470 --> 09:15.340
<i>Mine...</i>

09:15.680 --> 09:16.680
<i>And yours.</i>

09:17.140 --> 09:17.970
Our son?

09:18.800 --> 09:20.390
You're telling me I have a son?

09:21.220 --> 09:23.060
<i>So then that was...</i>

09:23.060 --> 09:24.890
<i>My son entered
my consciousness.</i>

09:24.890 --> 09:26.060
That is incorrect.

09:26.520 --> 09:31.860
If you say you saw him, then you just
happened to look in my mind.

09:32.360 --> 09:35.400
<i>But I'm certain I met that boy.</i>

09:36.160 --> 09:37.910
You said you couldn't
see his face.

09:38.530 --> 09:39.580
That's natural.

09:40.580 --> 09:43.540
<i>Because Takeo is already gone.</i>

09:44.830 --> 09:45.920
What does that mean?

09:49.170 --> 09:52.340
Do you mean he's dead?

09:54.550 --> 09:58.430
Someday I'll tell you everything.

09:59.430 --> 10:02.220
But for now, please stop
meddling in my affairs.

10:20.240 --> 10:21.620
Staying here is pointless.

10:22.240 --> 10:24.450
In the meantime,
let's go back to the Sasaki house.

10:32.920 --> 10:33.800
An avalanche?

10:35.460 --> 10:37.010
Doesn't seem like it.

10:38.760 --> 10:41.220
Is a mountain monster
making snowmen or...

10:44.430 --> 10:46.520
What on earth is that?

10:47.100 --> 10:50.060
It seems that snowman
has business with us.

10:51.270 --> 10:53.440
So let's go say hello!

10:54.320 --> 10:54.980
Wait!

11:13.790 --> 11:14.590
What's that?

11:15.420 --> 11:16.210
Storm.

11:20.220 --> 11:21.840
There's one here, too.

11:24.640 --> 11:27.100
Greetings, ladies and
gentlemen of the X-Men.

11:27.730 --> 11:29.230
How do you like Japan?

11:29.850 --> 11:31.230
It's not bad.

11:31.850 --> 11:34.520
The food is good and
the scenery's nice.

11:34.520 --> 11:38.530
Then you'll have no regrets
when I kill you here!

11:40.280 --> 11:43.450
Sorry, but I haven't seen
any Kabuki yet.

12:19.030 --> 12:19.990
What are you?

12:19.990 --> 12:21.950
Some kind of hedgehog monster?

12:31.910 --> 12:32.460
Beast!

12:33.540 --> 12:35.000
Did you pulverize him?

12:35.830 --> 12:37.090
There was no resistance.

12:38.300 --> 12:40.090
You are pretty tough.

12:42.510 --> 12:43.760
It's about time.

12:43.970 --> 12:44.970
What?

12:49.680 --> 12:52.060
So that was the aim of
the attack just now.

12:52.480 --> 12:54.350
The greetings are finished.

12:54.650 --> 12:55.650
Let's meet again.

12:56.480 --> 12:57.610
I see.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.940
He can liquefy his body.

13:00.610 --> 13:02.400
That's why he offered
no resistance.

13:02.400 --> 13:03.950
This is no time for analysis!

13:04.360 --> 13:05.280
Let's get out of here!

13:33.350 --> 13:34.350
Jun?

13:35.100 --> 13:37.150
I'm going to take
my shot in my room.

13:37.190 --> 13:39.110
Make sure the X-Men
don't see you.

13:39.110 --> 13:40.070
Be careful.

13:40.730 --> 13:41.940
I understand.

13:55.250 --> 13:56.000
Hisako?

13:56.830 --> 13:58.710
Is something wrong
with your right hand?

14:00.460 --> 14:02.050
The bruise on my hand is hurting.

14:02.500 --> 14:03.130
Bruise?

14:05.470 --> 14:07.800
It used to be bigger.

14:08.510 --> 14:10.800
Do you remember
an injury or a burn?

14:11.260 --> 14:12.100
No.

14:12.100 --> 14:14.850
Mom and Dad also say
they don't remember it,

14:14.850 --> 14:16.850
so I thought it was
just a birthmark.

14:17.940 --> 14:20.400
It suddenly started hurting
when I got here.

14:21.150 --> 14:23.190
Has it ever hurt you
like this before?

14:23.780 --> 14:24.900
I don't think so.

14:25.530 --> 14:26.860
That's strange,

14:26.860 --> 14:28.860
I wonder if something irritated it.

14:33.330 --> 14:34.120
I...

14:34.120 --> 14:37.210
I'm going to ask Dr. Sasaki
for an ointment.

14:37.580 --> 14:38.040
Hey!

14:38.710 --> 14:41.630
She told us to use
the intercom, remember?

14:41.630 --> 14:42.460
It's all right.

14:43.130 --> 14:45.380
It's not as if she's going outside.

14:45.710 --> 14:46.470
But...

14:46.970 --> 14:50.300
This is a good opportunity.
I need to talk to you.

14:56.270 --> 14:57.020
Talk?

15:03.940 --> 15:06.860
<i>Blackbird auto-pilot engaged.</i>

15:07.610 --> 15:09.280
<i>Launch preparations complete.</i>

15:26.960 --> 15:29.220
You want me to
let you read my mind?

15:29.630 --> 15:30.130
Yes.

15:30.880 --> 15:31.890
What for?

15:32.850 --> 15:36.140
To remove your hesitation.

15:36.140 --> 15:37.520
My hesitation?

15:38.520 --> 15:42.150
I heard you couldn't fight
the berserk mutant

15:42.150 --> 15:44.480
at the U-Men base and
almost lost your life.

15:45.360 --> 15:47.320
Is it because of Jean?

15:49.400 --> 15:54.120
The Professor proved I had nothing
to do with Jean's death.

15:54.580 --> 15:56.740
So what is making you suffer?

15:58.790 --> 16:00.660
Hisako also asked me.

16:01.250 --> 16:03.460
"Help him," she said.

16:04.040 --> 16:05.500
It's none of her business.

16:06.130 --> 16:09.210
She's worried about you
in her own way.

16:11.470 --> 16:14.800
And I also don't want a leader
who's so hesitant.

16:15.760 --> 16:20.230
At this rate, it may impede
our work as X-Men.

16:21.230 --> 16:23.100
Face your heart.

16:24.020 --> 16:26.520
I'm sure Jean would
wish for that, too.

16:33.450 --> 16:35.620
I don't like this.

16:35.620 --> 16:36.620
What's wrong?

16:37.530 --> 16:41.210
Yui Sasaki said she introduced us
to everyone in the mansion.

16:41.660 --> 16:44.420
But I can still smell someone
else in there.

16:46.000 --> 16:47.290
Indeed.

16:47.290 --> 16:49.960
She doesn't seem
to want us there.

16:50.800 --> 16:54.930
Yui Sasaki's presence at the center
of the mutant phenomena

16:54.930 --> 16:58.930
and the appearance of the U-Men seems
a bit too much for coincidence.

17:01.140 --> 17:04.440
Seems we'd better
keep an eye on Yui Sasaki.

17:05.190 --> 17:08.360
That's why I asked
Scott and Emma to stay.

17:25.460 --> 17:26.250
<i>Scott.</i>

17:27.330 --> 17:30.420
<i>The X-Men are
a light for mutants.</i>

17:30.420 --> 17:32.710
<i>I want to become that light.</i>

17:33.840 --> 17:38.220
<i>I want to brighten the future, for mutant
and human children all over the world...</i>

17:49.520 --> 17:50.730
<i>I'm begging you, Scott.</i>

17:51.320 --> 17:52.610
<i>Kill me.</i>

17:53.030 --> 17:54.990
<i>You know I could never do that!</i>

17:57.160 --> 17:58.030
<i>You...</i>

17:58.950 --> 18:00.490
<i>What did you do
to Jean's heart?</i>

18:04.370 --> 18:07.460
I love you, Scott...

18:09.750 --> 18:10.540
Jean!

18:24.390 --> 18:25.350
You are?

18:28.150 --> 18:29.350
Now you die, too.

18:36.740 --> 18:37.860
Scott.

18:59.050 --> 19:00.550
Dr. Sasaki?

19:03.560 --> 19:04.680
Feeling better?

19:05.600 --> 19:06.020
Yeah.

19:09.730 --> 19:11.690
The shadow you saw
behind Jean,

19:12.400 --> 19:14.480
it's natural that
you'd think it was me.

19:16.280 --> 19:19.200
I was attacked by myself.

19:20.280 --> 19:21.370
What on earth was that?

19:22.070 --> 19:24.790
That must have been
your subconscious,

19:24.790 --> 19:29.040
the part of your mind where you can't forgive
yourself for not saving Jean.

19:33.460 --> 19:34.250
I...

19:35.210 --> 19:41.220
tried to escape my inability to save Jean
by blaming you for her death.

19:42.800 --> 19:46.810
You're right, the one person
I can't forgive is myself.

19:50.270 --> 19:53.110
Now that I know you had nothing to do
with Jean's death,

19:53.730 --> 19:55.230
what should I do?

19:56.230 --> 20:00.200
One year ago, if I'd been there
when Jean went berserk,

20:00.700 --> 20:02.610
I might have been able
to save her.

20:03.450 --> 20:04.370
And you, as well.

20:09.250 --> 20:10.710
Listen to me, Scott.

20:11.580 --> 20:15.380
Aren't you the one
who taught Hisako

20:15.380 --> 20:17.630
that an X-Man's most important
quality is his heart?

20:18.550 --> 20:22.180
You need a stronger heart
than anyone else.

20:23.390 --> 20:26.640
Don't let Jean's will go to waste.

20:30.810 --> 20:33.100
<i>I want to become that light.</i>

20:34.100 --> 20:34.980
<i>And I...</i>

20:34.980 --> 20:38.690
<i>I want to continue shining alight
on the future for human and mutant children.</i>

20:43.160 --> 20:44.870
So now you want to coach me,

20:47.280 --> 20:50.120
just like Hisako?

23:03.380 --> 23:08.510
The beast that suddenly appeared in the lab
turns out to have an unexpected identity.

23:09.220 --> 23:14.060
Amid the confusion, Emma becomes
suspicious of Yui Sasaki's assistant Jun.

23:14.560 --> 23:16.600
Mean while,
danger approaches Professor X

23:16.600 --> 23:21.520
as he flies to Tohoku
from New York on the Blackbird.

23:22.690 --> 23:25.190
A new facet of
the case is revealed.

23:26.820 --> 23:29.780
Next time on X-Men: Lost

23:26.860 --> 23:31.070
<b><i>Lost - Omen</i></b>
